# The HTTP corpus is HTTP: every request line and header ends CRLF, and the
# repository .gitattributes says `text=auto eol=lf`, which would rewrite those
# CRLFs to LF on commit and leave the seeds no longer valid requests.  `-text`
# turns every conversion off for the corpus, in both directions.
#
# 量 2026-09-30: without this line `git ls-files --eol` reports `i/none w/crlf`
# for nine of the fourteen HTTP seeds, which is git saying it intends to convert
# them.  With it they read `i/-text w/-text`.
corpus/** -text
